        "original_id": "88f8446e-3fd3-56df-a6f5-fb30e321b6ba",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Charles Lane, Lucille Ball, Jim Brochu, Steve Schalchlin, John Bettis, Marie Cain\n- Works: I Love Lucy, The Lucy–Desi Comedy Hour, The Lucy Show, Here's Lucy, Life with Lucy, Lucy in the Afternoon, The Last Session, MythBusters\n- Roles: supporting actor, authority figure, comedic foe, author\n\nFacts:\n- Lucille Ball was best known as the star of the self-produced sitcoms \"I Love Lucy,\" \"The Lucy–Desi Comedy Hour,\" \"The Lucy Show,\" \"Here's Lucy,\" and \"Life with Lucy.\"\n- Charles Lane was a favored supporting actor of Lucille Ball on \"I Love Lucy,\" \"The Lucy–Desi Comedy Hour,\" and \"The Lucy Show.\"\n- Charles Lane often played a no-nonsense authority figure and comedic foe to Lucille Ball's scatterbrained TV character.\n- Jim Brochu was a friend of Lucille Ball.\n- Jim Brochu wrote the unauthorized biography \"Lucy in the Afternoon.\"\n- Jim Brochu appeared on an episode of \"MythBusters\" in his capacity as the author of \"Lucy in the Afternoon.\"\n- \"The Last Session\" is a musical with a book by Jim Brochu, music and lyrics by Steve Schalchlin, and additional lyrics by John Bettis and Marie Cain.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
